        content: 'Metal Arms: Glitch in the System is a third-person shooter video game developed by Swingin\' Ape Studios and published by Sierra Entertainment. Released in 2003, this game invites players to step into the metallic shoes of Glitch, a robot freedom fighter battling for the freedom of the planet Iron Star against the villainous General Corrosive and his army of Mils. Metal Arms offers a unique blend of shooting, driving, and puzzle-solving gameplay. Players navigate a fully destructible, futuristic world while commanding an array of weaponry and controlling different vehicles. One of the key gameplay features is the ability to control defeated enemies, thereby using their abilities and weapons to progress. The game is recognized for its fast-paced action, diverse gameplay, humor, and a grand sense of scale, as players battle their way through vast environments. Additionally, it features multiple multiplayer modes, ranging from traditional deathmatches to creative new modes focused on robotic combat. If you\'re a fan of action-packed, dynamic gameplay titles like Ratchet & Clank and Star Wars Battlefront, you\'ll be a fan of Metal Arms: Glitch in the System.',
