        content: 'Shadowgate is a point-and-click adventure game developed by ICOM Simulations and published by Kemco. First released in 1987, the game casts players as a brave adventurer tasked with exploring the titular castle, Shadowgate, to halt a looming apocalypse prophesied by an ancient riddle. Gameplay in Shadowgate primarily involves puzzle-solving, exploration, and inventory management. Players interact with the environment by selecting commands like \'Open\', \'Close\', \'Get\', and \'Look\' and applying them to objects to progress through the game\'s numerous rooms. Each room is a puzzle offering its unique sets of traps and mystical creatures. A unique feature of the game is the presence of \'Torches\', which cast light in the room. Letting them burn out can result in the player dying in darkness, adding a sense of urgency and tension. Shadowgate has been lauded for its atmospheric presentation, intricate puzzle design, and unique use of light mechanics. If you\'re a fan of point-and-click adventure games like King\'s Quest or Detective-like puzzle games such as L.A. Noire, you\'ll be a fan of Shadowgate.',
