        content: "DuckTales is a platform video game developed and published by Capcom based on the Disney animated TV series of the same name. It was first released on the Nintendo Entertainment System in 1989, letting players control Scrooge McDuck on a globe-trotting adventure. The gameplay of DuckTales involves traveling to different parts of the world and collecting treasures to become the world's richest duck. Scrooge can attack enemies and get around using his cane; notably, he can bounce on it like a pogo stick to defeat enemies, cross hazards or reach higher areas. The game stands out for its non-linear gameplay, which allows players to choose and complete levels in any order they wish. DuckTales received widespread critical acclaim for its stellar controls, vibrant visuals, captivating music, and charming plot based on the beloved cartoon series. It is considered to be among the best video games on the NES platform. If you are fond of adventurous platform games such as Super Mario Bros. or Chip'n Dale: Rescue Rangers, you'll be a fan of DuckTales.",
