        content: "Vib-Ribbon is a rhythm-based platformer developed by NanaOn-Sha and released in 1999 for the PlayStation. The game is renowned for its minimalist yet charming design, featuring a hand-drawn aesthetic and a unique premise that stands out in the rhythm game genre. Players control Vibri, a quirky, rabbit-like character, as they traverse an ever-changing obstacle course generated by the beats and rhythms of the game's soundtrack. Vib-Ribbon is particularly noteworthy for its innovative ability to generate levels from any audio CD inserted into the PlayStation, allowing players to create personalized experiences based on their favorite music. The gameplay revolves around timing button presses to navigate obstacles such as loops, waves, spikes, and pits that correspond to the rhythm of the music, requiring precision and creativity as the challenges intensify with faster tracks. Despite its simplicity, Vib-Ribbon has been celebrated for its distinct visual style, engaging mechanics, and its groundbreaking feature of integrating player-chosen audio into the gameplay. If you're a fan of rhythm games like Parappa the Rapper or Rez, you'll be a fan of Vib-Ribbon.",
