        content: "Contrast is a puzzle-platformer developed by Compulsion Games and released in 2013. Set in a dreamlike, 1920s-inspired world filled with jazz and vaudeville, the game follows a young girl named Didi and her imaginary friend Dawn, who has the unique ability to shift between the three-dimensional physical world and two-dimensional shadow realms. Players control Dawn as they help Didi uncover the secrets behind her fractured family and her mother's troubled relationship with her elusive father. The gameplay revolves around manipulating light and shadows to solve puzzles, as Dawn can use shadows on walls as platforms to traverse otherwise inaccessible areas. This mechanic is central to the game and creates inventive platforming challenges that blend seamlessly with its noir aesthetic. Contrast stands out for its striking art style, evocative music, and emotional story, which touches on themes of family, love, and abandonment. Its shadow-shifting mechanic adds a distinct layer of gameplay, setting it apart from traditional platformers. If you're a fan of atmospheric puzzle-platformers like Limbo or Braid, you'll be a fan of Contrast.",
