        content: "Titanic: Adventure Out of Time is a point-and-click adventure game developed by CyberFlix and released in 1996. Set aboard a meticulously recreated virtual version of the infamous RMS Titanic, the game places players in the role of Frank Carlson, a British secret agent who gets a second chance to alter crucial historical events after his failed mission leads to catastrophic consequences. Following a time-travel twist, Carlson awakens in 1912, just before the Titanic sets sail, and must navigate the ship's grand interiors, interact with its richly detailed characters, and complete espionage-related objectives to change the course of history. The gameplay focuses on exploration, puzzle-solving, and dialogue-driven interactions, with choices and actions directly influencing the outcome of the story and the fate of key characters. The game is highly praised for its historical authenticity, vividly recreating the luxurious interiors of the Titanic and blending them with an engaging alternate-history narrative. Titanic: Adventure Out of Time stands out for combining historical fiction with complex storytelling, marking it as a unique and memorable gaming experience. If you're a fan of narrative-rich adventure games like The Last Express or Myst, you'll be a fan of Titanic: Adventure Out of Time.",
