        content: "Frequency is a music rhythm game developed by Harmonix and published by SCEI, released in 2001 for the PlayStation 2. In this innovative title, players navigate a 3D, tunnel-like environment as they remix and play electronic tracks. The gameplay revolves around activating note patterns on different instrument tracks of a song, such as drums, bass, vocals, and synth, by timing button presses to align with the beat. Successfully completing sequences on a track temporarily locks it into autopilot, allowing players to shift focus to other tracks and fully assemble the song. The game features a rich library of electronic and hip-hop tracks from popular artists of the time, as well as an option to remix songs using its built-in editor. Frequency's mesmerizing visuals and fast-paced gameplay create an addictive and immersive rhythmic experience. It stands out for its emphasis on creativity and its ability to make players feel like they're building and performing music. With its blend of challenging reflex-based mechanics and engaging musical composition, Frequency is a game that both rhythm fans and music lovers can appreciate. If you're a fan of rhythm-focused games like Amplitude or Beat Saber, you'll be a fan of Frequency.",
