        content: "Gex is a platformer developed by Crystal Dynamics and released in 1995 for multiple systems. Players take control of Gex, a wisecracking gecko with a taste for television, as he embarks on a mission to escape the clutches of the evil cybernetic entity known as Rez. Gex is sucked into the Media Dimension, a surreal world filled with environments inspired by various TV genres, such as horror, cartoons, and kung fu. The gameplay revolves around classic 2D platforming mechanics, with Gex navigating diverse levels, defeating enemies, and collecting remote controls that unlock new areas. A standout feature of Gex is his ability to stick to walls and ceilings, adding a unique twist to the platforming action. The game is packed with humor, with Gex delivering a constant stream of witty pop culture references and one-liners, voiced by comedian Dana Gould in the original version. Gex was praised for its colorful visuals, varied level design, and its charm as a mascot-driven platformer during the 90s. If you\u2019re a fan of classic platformers like Earthworm Jim or Rayman, you\u2019ll be a fan of Gex.",
