                content: "Metal Gear, released in 1987 by Konami and created by Hideo Kojima, is a pioneering stealth action-adventure game that introduced players to tactical espionage gameplay. Set in the fictional country of Outer Heaven, players take on the role of Solid Snake, a rookie operative of the special forces unit FOXHOUND, tasked with infiltrating a military fortress to destroy a secret weapon known as Metal Gear, a bipedal walking tank capable of launching nuclear missiles. The gameplay emphasizes stealth over direct combat, requiring players to evade enemies, gather key items, and strategically complete objectives while minimizing detection. Innovative for its time, Metal Gear introduced the concept of avoiding sightlines and creating paths through enemy terrain rather than simply engaging in firefights, setting the foundation for an entire genre. Its focus on narrative-driven missions, iconic characters, and immersive gameplay mechanics made it a standout title of its era. Metal Gear has since become a landmark in video game history, influencing countless games that followed. If you're a fan of stealth-based games like Splinter Cell or Deus Ex, you'll be a fan of Metal Gear.",
